  "id": "f-statistic",
  "term": "F statistic",
  "definition": "The F statistic is a statistical value used to test whether group effects differ more than would be expected by chance in designs such as one-way and split-plot studies. In the source, its performance is described as generally resistant to non-normal data and often robust when variances are equal, but more affected when group variances differ and group sizes are unequal, especially depending on how large variances are paired with large or small groups.",
